{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1bAxZu7FFVZSMdX5t24z9","type":"tool_result","content":"95\t  - **vi.spyOn on a re-exported barrel function** (`vi.spyOn(connectorModule, 'selectConnector')`) only intercepts calls that go through the imported symbol, not direct calls inside the module. Because the route handler imports `selectConnector` from `@/lib/lessonChat/connector` and the test imports the same module, the spy works without `vi.mock(...)`. Same pattern as the existing `api.test.ts` — keep the alias path consistent.\n96\t  - **Playwright `run.js` leaves `.temp-execution-<ts>.js` artifacts** in `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/`. Not gitignored; show up as untracked in `git status` after a browser run. Delete them before committing.\n97\t  - **Lesson chat history field is plumbed end-to-end but unused by the prompt assembly stub.** The route accepts `history: Array<{role, content}>` and the connector signature receives it via `ConnectorRequest`, but `assemblePrompt` only uses `message`. Wiring history (and `sectionId` lesson context) into the actual prompt is US-054. Don't drop the history-collection code in the component when working on US-054 — just teach `assemblePrompt` to consume it.\n98\t  - **For UI tags requiring backend, run `npm run dev` then point playwright at it.** Detection helper missed the server initially (per the existing playwright skill note); just hardcode `TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3000/...'` in the test script. The dev server starts cleanly in <300ms with Turbopack.\n99\t---\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac2e4d8e-61f9-4667-9e24-a812af5dbc90","uuid":"d5bdd97e-c547-4337-80ad-989543a53c86","timestamp":"2026-05-04T06:46:09.188Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-054/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"  - **vi.spyOn on a re-exported barrel function** (`vi.spyOn(connectorModule, 'selectConnector')`) only intercepts calls that go through the imported symbol, not direct calls inside the module. Because the route handler imports `selectConnector` from `@/lib/lessonChat/connector` and the test imports the same module, the spy works without `vi.mock(...)`. Same pattern as the existing `api.test.ts` — keep the alias path consistent.\n  - **Playwright `run.js` leaves `.temp-execution-<ts>.js` artifacts** in `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/`. Not gitignored; show up as untracked in `git status` after a browser run. Delete them before committing.\n  - **Lesson chat history field is plumbed end-to-end but unused by the prompt assembly stub.** The route accepts `history: Array<{role, content}>` and the connector signature receives it via `ConnectorRequest`, but `assemblePrompt` only uses `message`. Wiring history (and `sectionId` lesson context) into the actual prompt is US-054. Don't drop the history-collection code in the component when working on US-054 — just teach `assemblePrompt` to consume it.\n  - **For UI tags requiring backend, run `npm run dev` then point playwright at it.** Detection helper missed the server initially (per the existing playwright skill note); just hardcode `TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3000/...'` in the test script. The dev server starts cleanly in <300ms with Turbopack.\n---\n","numLines":6,"startLine":95,"totalLines":100}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JVXPowV43jqSMREo8RY9ii","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013cvHAejvcK7GtLAqGQnpeW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-054/scripts/ralph/progress.txt << 'EOF'\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-054\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts` exporting `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId? }) → { systemPrompt, contextBlock }`. `systemPrompt` is the spec-mandated string verbatim. `contextBlock` always leads with `Lesson title: …\\nEyebrow: …\\nDescription: …\\nEstimated minutes: …`. When `currentSectionId` resolves to a real section, the active section is serialised per type (theory→`markdown`; quiz→question + numbered options; code→`taskMarkdown` + `starterCode`; codeCloze→`taskMarkdown`+template; sandbox/demo/histogram/plotImage/parametricExplorer/dragMatch/dataTable/video/custom→short type-specific summary). When `currentSectionId` is omitted or unknown, falls back to `Lesson outline:\\n- [<type>] <title>` lines. If the assembled string exceeds `CONTEXT_CHAR_LIMIT` (4000) the body portion is truncated and `'… [truncated]'` appended; the lesson header is preserved.\n- Wired `src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts` to load the lesson via `lessonFile()` + `LessonSchema.parse()`, call `buildPromptContext({ lesson, currentSectionId: req.body.sectionId })`, and pass `{ systemPrompt, userMessage: '<contextBlock>\\n\\nUser question: <message>', history }` to the connector. New 404 path when the lesson file is missing; 500 when stored JSON fails schema.\n- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts` interface: `ConnectorRequest` now `{ systemPrompt?, userMessage, history? }` (was `{ message, history? }`). Both `subprocessConnector` and `agentSdkConnector` pass `assemblePrompt(req.userMessage, req.systemPrompt)` to the underlying CLI/SDK. `assemblePrompt` retains a default fallback prompt for direct callers/tests.\n- `src/components/LessonChat.tsx` now tracks the active section via IntersectionObserver. Effect runs when `open` flips true; observes every `[data-section-id]` element with `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` so only the strip near the top of the viewport counts as \"active\". Picks the highest-DOM-order intersecting section so when several straddle the band we keep the one the learner has scrolled into. Seeds an initial `activeSectionId` from current scroll position so the first message after opening has a value before IO fires. Wraps in a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` so sections rendered AFTER the panel opens (lesson loads async) get observed too. The fetch POST now includes `sectionId: activeSectionId ?? undefined`. Panel exposes `data-active-section-id={activeSectionId ?? ''}` for tests.\n- Added `src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts` (8 tests): systemPrompt verbatim, lesson metadata in contextBlock, theory-section body, quiz question+numbered options, code task+starter, outline fallback when sectionId omitted, outline fallback when sectionId unknown, truncation when content exceeds 4000 chars.\n- Updated `src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts` to write a fake lesson under a `mkdtempSync` `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` so the new disk read works; also added a \"passes systemPrompt + contextBlock-derived userMessage to connector\" test that captures the connector's `chat()` arg and checks for `Lesson title:`, the section markdown, and `User question: <text>` substrings. Plus a 404 case when the lesson file is missing.\n- Updated existing `src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts` to use the new `userMessage` field in place of `message`.\n- Files changed: src/lib/lessonChat/context.ts (new); src/lib/lessonChat/context.test.ts (new); src/app/api/lesson-chat/route.ts (modified — fetches lesson, builds context); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.ts (modified — ConnectorRequest shape); src/lib/lessonChat/connector.test.ts (modified — userMessage); src/lib/lessonChat/route.test.ts (modified — disk fixture + new assertions); src/components/LessonChat.tsx (modified — IO + MO + sectionId in POST).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 200/200 (added 9 new tests across context.test.ts and route.test.ts). `npm run lint` baseline 163/25 unchanged from US-053. Browser test (`/tmp/playwright-test-US-054.js`, 8 assertions) passes against the real `claude -p` subprocess: navigates to seed lesson, opens chat panel, programmatically scrolls main content so quiz section `s2-quiz-kernel` reaches the top, waits for `data-active-section-id` to flip to that id, sends \"What is this question testing?\", confirms POST body includes `sectionId: 's2-quiz-kernel'`, and validates the assistant reply explicitly references the **kernel** quiz topic (\"This question is testing whether you understand the **definition of a kernel** in image filtering — specifically, that it's a small matrix of weights used in the convolution operation.\"). Screenshot at /tmp/US-054-after-send.png.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **IntersectionObserver vs late-rendering targets.** When the chat panel opens immediately after navigation, the `useEffect` may run before the lesson page has fetched its data and rendered `[data-section-id]` elements. A first-pass `document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-id]')` returns 0. The fix is twofold: (a) observe what's currently mounted, (b) wrap a `MutationObserver` on `document.body` (`{childList: true, subtree: true}`) and re-call `observeAllSections()` on each mutation, with a `WeakSet<Element>` to avoid double-observing. The old \"queryAll once in useEffect\" pattern only works when the parent's content is statically rendered before the effect runs.\n  - **rootMargin trick for \"section-at-the-top\" detection.** `rootMargin: '0px 0px -75% 0px'` shrinks the IntersectionObserver root rect so only the top 25% of the viewport counts as \"intersecting\". Combined with picking the highest-DOM-order intersecting section, you reliably get \"what is the user reading right now\". A naive ratio-based pick gets fooled by big sections (a long theory section with ratio 0.6 wins over a small quiz with ratio 1.0).\n  - **vitest + COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE for route handlers that touch fs.** The lesson-chat route now reads from disk. To test it without polluting `courses/`, snapshot the env var, point it at a `mkdtempSync(...)` dir, write a single fake lesson JSON inside `<root>/<courseSlug>/lessons/<lessonSlug>.json`, and restore the env var in `afterAll`. `assertSafeSlug` in `paths.ts` is happy with the slugs `c` / `l` so the fixture file path is just `<tmp>/c/lessons/l.json`.\n  - **Connector signature is an internal contract — break it freely between US-053 and US-054.** Renaming `ConnectorRequest.message → userMessage` and adding `systemPrompt?` was the cleanest expression of \"the route now owns prompt assembly\". Updating the existing test fixture's `message: 'hi'` → `userMessage: 'hi'` was a one-pass `sed`. Don't try to keep both shapes for backwards compatibility — the connector has exactly one consumer (the API route) so the bridge is invisible.\n  - **Playwright skill `run.js` requires the script to self-wrap.** A `module.exports = async ({ chromium }) => {...}` pattern silently no-ops because the wrapper only auto-wraps inline code; for file mode it just `require()`s the file and assumes the script self-executes. Use the existing US-053 pattern: `const { chromium } = require('playwright'); (async () => { ... })().catch(...)`. The wrapper documents this in the auto-wrap branch only — a script that lacks the `(async () => {` token but has `require(` is run as-is.\n  - **playwright `waitForSelector('...[data-open=\"true\"]')` doesn't poll attribute changes well.** Even when the attribute is set in the same render commit as the element appearing, the visibility check sometimes flakes. Prefer `page.waitForFunction(() => el.getAttribute('data-open') === 'true')` for attribute transitions — same pattern as the US-052 close-state assertion learning.\n  - **Test cleanup matters before browser runs in dev.** localStorage state from the prior US-053 run (`lessonChat-open`, `lessonChatDraft:…`) survives across reloads and test runs because the dev server points at the same origin. The US-054 playwright test removes both keys in-page before the explicit reload, otherwise the chat panel opens unexpectedly and the `tutor-btn` toggle inverts.\n---\nEOF\necho \"appended\"\nwc -l /home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-054/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","description":"Append US-054 progress entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":166475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":697},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac2e4d8e-61f9-4667-9e24-a812af5dbc90","uuid":"882cd07d-c700-4021-a870-f99014d9ffc9"}
